# LM35 Temperature-Based Fire Alarm

## Description
An Arduino-based fire/overheat alarm system that uses an LM35 temperature sensor 
to continuously monitor ambient temperature. When the temperature crosses a set 
threshold, a buzzer is triggered as an alert.

## Components Used
- Arduino Uno R3
- LM35 Temperature Sensor
- Buzzer

## Circuit Connections
| Component | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| LM35 (OUT) | Analog Pin A1 |
| Buzzer (+) | Digital Pin 8 |

## How It Works
1. The LM35 sensor continuously outputs an analog voltage proportional to temperature.
2. The Arduino reads this value and converts it to degrees Celsius.
3. The temperature is printed to the Serial Monitor every second.
4. If temperature reaches or exceeds 45°C, the buzzer turns ON.
5. If temperature drops below 45°C, the buzzer turns OFF.

